Project conventions win. Read the neighbouring tests first.

## Placement

❌ __tests__/checklist_card.test.tsx
✅ checklist_card.tsx + checklist_card.test.tsx
Colocated beside the source. No `__tests__` directories.

`describe('<ExportedSymbol>')` at the top level, one nested `describe` per method or option group.

## Naming

❌ it('should throw a 409 error when the state blocks activity')
✅ it('throws a 409 error in a state that blocks activity')
Declarative third person. No "should".

## Mocking

✅ const makeService = (state: TMaintenanceState) =>
     ({ getState: jest.fn(async () => state) } as unknown as IMaintenanceService);
Services and anything stateful get a hand-rolled fake that round-trips state: a client that throws
NotFound until `create`, an API that tracks `enabled` so pause then resume behaves. Cast at the seam
with `as unknown as T`, and JSDoc each option field.

✅ jest.mock('../../hooks/use_services', () => ({ useServices: () => stub }));
`jest.mock` is for module-mocking your own hooks in component tests. Not for services.

✅ const REQUEST = {} as IRequest;
Shared fixtures are SCREAMING_SNAKE module constants.

Variables get full names here too: `ordersClient`, not `rc`.

## Assertions

❌ expect(result).toMatchSnapshot();
✅ await expect(assertNotPaused({ service, request: REQUEST })).rejects.toMatchObject({ statusCode: 409 });
✅ expect(service.getStatus).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
Concrete values, or `expect.objectContaining`. Snapshots only where a tool generates them.
Negative assertions pin what must not happen, such as proving a guard took the cheap read.

## What to test

Whether a test is worth writing at all is decided by `test-value.mdc`: behaviour that can break, no
assertions against copies of the code or config, nothing that passes with the implementation deleted.
Once a test passes that bar, this file says how to write it.

Edge cases and contracts first; the happy path only as their setup. Idempotency, retry after partial
failure, a missing dependency, out-of-band state change, inverted ranges, and the exact boundary
(299ms, then 300ms).
